{"type": "message", "id": "8b0b3159", "parentId": "981079df", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T06:42:18.463Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "tool-b45564d26baf42cc8f08d04bede15c71", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Eurostat suicides railway 2014 2020 Germany 800 France 300 Netherlands Belgium numbers\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 902,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0bd46e513acafa2f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0bd46e513acafa2f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ecc5fc957d46e7c4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSuicides occurring on railways are reported separately from people killed or injured in railway accidents. For the EU as a whole, the number of such suicides remained <strong>between 2 200 and 2 800 per year in the period 2010-2024</strong>. The highest number was recorded in 2012 with 2 734 suicides on railway ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ecc5fc957d46e7c4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9154ca9d72b62867\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9154ca9d72b62867\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd8aac8a5bedd262\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>In 2024, the number of people killed in railway accidents in the EU fell to 750</strong>, a 10.8% decrease compared with 2023 (841 deaths) · The declining number of rail transport fatalities in 2024 came after 2 consecutive years of increases.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd8aac8a5bedd262\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7fd2726823c14cf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7fd2726823c14cf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df8eff66022f965f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df8eff66022f965f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ca094bdc19c0b50\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEU railway deaths fall in 2024\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ca094bdc19c0b50\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.globalrailwayreview.com/news/233725/railway-deaths-in-the-eu-fall-in-2024-after-years-of-fluctuating-trends/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be30868514e1b98d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>Germany recorded the highest number with 688, followed by France with 267 and the Netherlands with 186</strong>. The lowest numbers were observed in Lithuania with none, Greece with one, and Estonia with f